# docs/decisions.md is a dated, append-only log (see its own preamble). Every
# branch that records a decision appends at EOF, so two concurrent branches
# conflict there BY CONSTRUCTION, independent of content -- measured to be
# the single biggest cause of /land conflicts (lode-4jtc.1). git's built-in
# 'union' merge driver takes both sides' added lines and drops nothing that
# existed in the base, which is exactly the guarantee an append-only file
# needs and exactly what that file's no-silent-rewrite rule already requires.
# No merge.union.driver entry is needed in any .git/config -- 'union' is a
# NAME git recognizes natively, so this committed file is sufficient on its
# own and travels on the git wire like any other tracked content. See
# docs/decisions.md (search "lode-4jtc.1") for the full rationale, the
# rejected alternatives, and the accepted failure mode this introduces.
docs/decisions.md merge=union
